WEBVTT

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:03.000
Organizations cannot defend what they cannot observe.

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:07.040
Telemetry provides visibility into activity across the environment and gives security

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:10.250
teams evidence they can use to recognize suspicious behavior,

00:00:10.250 --> 00:00:13.965
investigate incidents, and understand whether safeguards are working as intended.

00:00:13.965 --> 00:00:16.000
Visibility improves operational decisions.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:19.245
Analysts can compare current activity with expected patterns,

00:00:19.245 --> 00:00:23.440
correlate events from multiple systems, establish timelines, and determine which users,

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:26.000
devices, applications, or resources may be involved.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:28.995
Without reliable data, teams are forced to rely on assumptions.

00:00:28.995 --> 00:00:32.970
Telemetry also helps organizations measure security effectiveness.

00:00:32.970 --> 00:00:35.995
Teams can evaluate whether important systems are reporting,

00:00:35.995 --> 00:00:40.000
whether detections receive the data they require, how quickly incidents are discovered,

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:42.995
and where blind spots or retention limits could weaken an investigation.

00:00:42.995 --> 00:00:45.255
More data is not automatically better.

00:00:45.255 --> 00:00:48.965
Effective programs collect telemetry for clear security and operational purposes.

00:00:48.965 --> 00:00:53.000
They balance visibility with cost, privacy, retention, system performance,

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:56.660
and analyst workload so that collection produces useful evidence rather than unmanaged

00:00:56.660 --> 00:00:56.965
volume.

00:00:56.965 --> 00:01:01.250
A practical visibility review starts with important services and plausible security

00:01:01.250 --> 00:01:02.000
questions.

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:05.680
Teams ask whether they could identify who accessed a resource, what changed,

00:01:05.680 --> 00:01:09.205
which systems communicated, and how far back they could investigate.

00:01:09.205 --> 00:01:13.150
Answers expose blind spots more clearly than a simple count of connected log sources and

00:01:13.150 --> 00:01:15.000
help leaders prioritize improvement work.
